From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_SUBMIT_STATS=1: statistics of submissions, deferred submissions, waits and the front's macro reads (drain design stage 1); nothing changes without or with it

Statistics only. With the switch (exact "1") three lines are logged every 10 s; nothing is
submitted, deferred or waited for differently, with or without it.

1. "EDEN_UP_SUBMIT_STATS in N s, F frames: S submissions: ...": submissions by who asked for them.
   The names are ZpassCut's sites (draws, astc, fence, fence flush, list copy, idle) and, for its
   "other", the callers without a SiteScope: finish (Scheduler::Finish), wait (Scheduler::Wait's own
   flush), present (RendererVulkan::Composite); what is left stays "other" (the buffer cache's host
   read flushes, mostly). Counted in Scheduler::SubmitExecution, so every real submission counts,
   also without EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_CUT_LOG. Per name: the waits for the GPU to finish such a
   submission (MasterSemaphore::Wait past its quick checks) and the waits of other threads for the
   submission itself (Scheduler::WaitSubmitted), each with its time. Last: how often
   Scheduler::WaitForSubmission gave up after 20 ms (it did so without a word).
2. "EDEN_UP_SUBMIT_STATS deferred: ...": how many flushes Scheduler::DeferFlush put off, how many
   deferred submissions went out, and per sender the count, mean and longest delay from the first
   put-off flush: the back's own idle, the idle hook asked for by a submission waiter / by a drain
   / by someone else, the fence manager outside the hook, the next flush, a finish, a wait.
3. "EDEN_UP_SUBMIT_STATS front macro reads: ...": Maxwell3D::FrontDmaRead per window: snapshot
   hits, misses by reason (the counters the function already keeps and prints every 262,144
   reads), reads of listed reports, narrowed reads, read-ahead reads and how many of them drained
   (pending word / unsynced), plain drains.

This names the submission call sites without the build's ELF (EDEN_GPU_SUBMIT_ORIGIN gives return
addresses). Not in it from the design note: "list entries that are pure macro data" (needs the
command list parser, a patch of its own), and the idle hook's askers in fence_manager.h and
vk_rasterizer.cpp, which stay "another requested hook": both files are compiled in parts by build
checks or rewritten by the front's build-time edits, and a statistics patch should not move those.
The driver's side (how long radv_ps5_queue_wait_seq waited) is lead-mesh-25 of the RADV series.

Touches no line the front's build-time edits anchor on (tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py for
vk_scheduler.h/.cpp and renderer_vulkan.cpp, headless/macro_native.cmake for maxwell_3d.cpp), and
none of the functions tools/check-vulkan-handoff.py compiles on their own.

